Correlation



The only difference between the regression slope and the correlation is that correlations are calculated by standardizing the covariance for both X and Y.


\[
\text{Correlation}(x,y) = \frac{\text{Covariance}(x,y)}{s_x s_y}
\]
\[\begin{align}

s_x &= \text{the sample standard deviation of x} \\
s_y &= \text{the sample standard deviation of y} \\


\end{align}
\]
